<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2136" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ămātrĭx</span></b> ,
			īcis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				female lover</i>, in an honorable and a dishonorable sense, <i>a mistress</i>, <i>sweetheart</i>
			(syn.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amans, amica): Sappho amatrix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					7, 69, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dicacula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					As. 3, 1, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Poen. 5, 5, 25</span></i>.—Used as
				adj.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amatrices aquae,</span>”
				<i>amorous</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					7, 15</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">10,
		4</span></i>.</div>
